# Tailwind CSS v4

- Tailwind v4 is configured in CSS. Use `@import "tailwindcss";` and `@theme { ... }` for tokens. Don't create `tailwind.config.js` unless the project already has one.
- Don't use `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;` (v3 syntax).
- Vite projects use the `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin; PostCSS projects use `@tailwindcss/postcss`.
- v3 → v4 renames: `shadow-sm` → `shadow-xs`, `shadow` → `shadow-sm`, `rounded-sm` → `rounded-xs`, `rounded` → `rounded-sm`, `blur-sm` → `blur-xs`, `outline-none` → `outline-hidden`, `ring` → `ring-3`.
- `bg-opacity-*` / `text-opacity-*` are gone: use `bg-black/50`.
- Default border colour is `currentColor`; specify `border-gray-200` etc. explicitly.
- Custom utilities use `@utility name { ... }`, not `@layer utilities`.
- Prefer utility classes in markup. Extract a component, not an `@apply` soup.
